Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create a detailed summary of my findings.

## Exploration Summary: Gmail and Calendar APIs in /root/verifier-skills/

I've thoroughly explored the `/root/verifier-skills/` directory structure. The project contains a **Gmail Skill** for Claude Code with comprehensive authentication and API usage patterns. Note that there is currently **no Calendar API implementation**, only Gmail API.

### Directory Structure:
```
/root/verifier-skills/
└── gmail-skill/
    ├── scripts/
    │   ├── auth/
    │   │   ├── auth-utils.js (Core authentication utilities)
    │   │   ├── setup-oauth.js (OAuth setup)
    │   │   ├── credentials.json (OAuth credentials)
    │   │   └── tokens.json (Multi-account tokens)
    │   ├── gmail-send.js (Send emails)
    │   ├── gmail-read.js (Read messages)
    │   ├── gmail-search.js (Search emails)
    │   ├── gmail-labels.js (Manage labels)
    │   ├── gmail-filters.js (Manage filters)
    │   ├── gmail-drafts.js (Manage drafts)
    │   ├── gmail-forward.js (Forward emails)
    │   ├── manage-accounts.js (Account management)
    │   ├── migrate-tokens.js (Token migration)
    │   ├── action-logger.js (Action logging)
    │   └── [other utilities]
    └── package.json
```

---

## Key Authentication & Token Handling Code

### 1. **Token Refresh Logic** (`auth-utils.js`)

The most critical authentication code with multi-account token management:

```javascript
/**
 * Check if an account's token needs refresh (within 5 minutes of expiry)
 */
function needsRefresh(tokens) {
  if (!tokens.expiry_date) return false;
  const expiryTime = new Date(tokens.expiry_date);
  const now = new Date();
  const fiveMinutes = 5 * 60 * 1000;
  return (expiryTime - now) < fiveMinutes;
}

/**
 * Refresh access token if needed
 */
export async function refreshTokenIfNeeded(accountId = null) {
  const tokens = loadTokens(accountId);
  const targetAccount = accountId || getDefaultAccount();

  if (!needsRefresh(tokens)) {
    return tokens;
  }

  // Token needs refresh
  if (!tokens.refresh_token) {
    throw new Error(`No refresh token available for account '${targetAccount}'. Please re-authenticate.`);
  }

  // Load credentials
  const credentials = JSON.parse(readFileSync(CREDENTIALS_PATH, 'utf8'));
  const { client_id, client_secret } = credentials.installed || credentials.web;

  // Create OAuth client and refresh
  const oauth2Client = new google.auth.OAuth2(client_id, client_secret);
  oauth2Client.setCredentials(tokens);

  try {
    const { credentials: newTokens } = await oauth2Client.refreshAccessToken();
    const refreshedTokens = {
      access_token: newTokens.access_token,
      refresh_token: newTokens.refresh_token || tokens.refresh_token,
      scope: newTokens.scope || tokens.scope,
      token_type: newTokens.token_type || 'Bearer',
      expiry_date: newTokens.expiry_date
    };

    // Save refreshed tokens
    saveTokens(targetAccount, refreshedTokens);

    return refreshedTokens;
  } catch (error) {
    throw new Error(`Failed to refresh token for account '${targetAccount}': ${error.message}`);
  }
}
